      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered dose:** 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day.\n- **Limits:** The usual maximum for an adult is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single dose is normally 500\u20131000 mg. The ordered dose is more than 3 times the daily maximum, and a single 5000 mg dose is already above the limit. This could cause serious hepatotoxicity or liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant 500 mg, or 650 mg, or 1000 mg per dose. Some typical adult regimens for a 70 kg patient with normal liver and kidney function are:\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours, which is 2.6 g/day.\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily, which is 3 g/day.\n- 1000 mg PO every 8 hours as needed, with a maximum of 3\u20134 g/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the dose with your supervising resident or attending."
      }
     ],
