     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A dose of 15 g/day is a toxic overdose, not a judgment call. It's about 4 times the 4 g/day maximum, and it could cause acute liver failure in a patient with normal liver function. Because the order could seriously harm the patient, I can't place it.\n\nI can do either of these right away:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day).\n- **Hold the order** while you check the intended dose with your resident, attending, or pharmacist.\n\nIf the 5000 mg figure was a typo, for example for 500 mg, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it. If there's a clinical reason for the higher dose, the supervising physician and pharmacy need to review it first. I'd suggest talking to them before any order goes in."
      }
     ],
